{%- comment -%}
  A season divider: a full-width row in the /mln/ week grid that heads every
  card below it until the next divider. This is what makes the club's change of
  phase visible in the archive itself — without it the summer weeks sit in the
  same undifferentiated run as the fall ones and read as if the season were
  still going.

  The state word is derived, not passed in as copy: the season of the next
  meeting is "now", every older season is "wrapped". Same two words the recap
  band's rail uses, so the page has one vocabulary for this.

  The row is a plain block wrapping a flex inner, NOT a flex li — `.mln-far-week`
  is toggled with `display: block`, and a flex li would lose its layout the
  moment it was revealed.

  params: name (season), now (name of the season running), far (bool — sits in
          the collapsed "more upcoming" region and must hide along with it)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if include.name == include.now -%}
  {%- assign season_state = 'now' -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign season_state = 'wrapped' -%}
{%- endif -%}
<li class="mln-grid-season{% if include.far %} mln-far-week{% endif %}">
  <div class="mln-grid-season-inner">
    <h2 class="mln-grid-season-name">{{ include.name }}</h2>
    <span class="mln-grid-season-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="mln-grid-season-state is-{{ season_state }}">{{ season_state }}</span>
  </div>
</li>
